WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.200
the nineteenth of November.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.560
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:12.920
Washington has widened its blockade of
Iran to cover ship-to-ship transfers,

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.400
and another tanker attack in the
Strait of Hormuz has left a crew member

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:20.680
missing. Even so, crude fell
about three percent on Wednesday,

7
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.560
as US stocks built across
crude, gasoline and distillates.

8
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.800
On the markets. Early Wednesday, Brent
traded at ninety-two dollars fifty

9
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.760
a barrel and West Texas Intermediate
at eighty-four dollars seventy,

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:36.053
before oil closed the day
about three percent lower.

11
00:00:36.187 --> 00:00:39.840
According to the EIA, US commercial
crude stocks rose three point four

12
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.080
million barrels in the week
to the thirteenth of November.

13
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.520
In Europe, gas storage was
seventy percent full on Tuesday,

14
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.000
down two tenths of a point on the day.

15
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.760
Starting with the blockade.

16
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.400
US Central Command issued an advisory
on Wednesday saying that ships

17
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:58.400
taking cargo at sea from vessels
loaded in Iran will now be treated as

18
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.800
trying to evade the US
blockade of Iranian ports.

19
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.040
Those ships could face action.

20
00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.800
Until now, enforcement covered
the Iranian ports themselves.

21
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.200
This goes after the transshipment
step that hides where a cargo came

22
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.800
from. Any tanker joining those
transfers now carries blockade risk.

23
00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.760
So do buyers further down
the chain, mainly in China,

24
00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:20.507
if the cargoes reach them.

25
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:24.027
The advisory doesn't say how
many cargoes it would catch.

26
00:01:24.053 --> 00:01:26.160
The strikes are running both ways.

27
00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.840
US officials say American aircraft
hit a missile launch site on Qeshm

28
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.600
Island on Tuesday, belonging to Iran's
Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps.

29
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.933
The Guard Corps says it had first
attacked a US military site in Bahrain.

30
00:01:38.987 --> 00:01:42.840
That claim comes only from Iran,
and no damage has been reported.

31
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.400
Gulf states have issued fresh warnings
to residents about incoming projectiles.

32
00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:51.240
In the strait itself, the Abu Dhabi
National Oil Company's shipping arm,

33
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.120
ADNOC Logistics and Services, confirmed
one of its vessels was attacked

34
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.920
while transiting Hormuz
on Tuesday evening.

35
00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.240
One crew member is unaccounted
for and eleven were injured.

36
00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.280
The rest were evacuated. The company
hasn't named the vessel or the attacker.

37
00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:10.400
Separately, the liquefied petroleum
gas carrier Tara Gas was still burning

38
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:14.920
and adrift off Musandam on Wednesday,
according to a navigational warning.

39
00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:18.320
India's foreign ministry says
twenty-four of its twenty-five crew are

40
00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.813
accounted for.

41
00:02:19.867 --> 00:02:23.973
With supertankers being targeted,
more crude is moving on smaller ships,

42
00:02:24.107 --> 00:02:25.920
mostly through ship-to-ship transfers.

43
00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.640
According to Vortexa, Suezmax and
Aframax tankers carried two million

44
00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.600
barrels a day out of
the strait in October.

45
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.080
That's the most since the war began.

46
00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.680
Each of those ships carries less than
half the load of a very large crude

47
00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:44.560
carrier, so the same exports tie
up more hulls and more transfers.

48
00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.720
And those transfers are exactly
what the new US advisory targets.

49
00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.880
Back to the price move. Traders
pointed to rising supply,

50
00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:56.000
a stronger dollar and
weaker appetite for risk.

51
00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:58.640
The EIA weekly data added to that.

52
00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.080
Gasoline stocks rose five
point two million barrels.

53
00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.400
Distillates added one point six
million, a second straight weekly build,

54
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:10.080
taking them to just under one
hundred and five million barrels.

55
00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:13.760
Refineries ran at ninety-five
point seven percent of capacity,

56
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.160
up half a point. Total commercial
petroleum stocks rose nine point two

57
00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.600
million barrels. Crude
stocks, for what it's worth,

58
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.640
are still three percent
below the five-year average.

59
00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:28.240
Turning to refining, where diesel
is doing the heavy lifting.

60
00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.200
In a note dated the fifteenth of November,

61
00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.880
Kpler estimated that Ukrainian drone
strikes are keeping about three

62
00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.960
point nine million barrels a
day of Russian refining offline.

63
00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.160
That's well above the two point two
million figure in earlier Reuters

64
00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.760
reporting. Kpler also expects Russian
diesel exports to fall short of

65
00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.200
the planned two million tonnes.

66
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:53.360
With less Russian gasoil on the water,
gasoil is leading a margin rally

67
00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.680
while gasoline and naphtha lag.

68
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:58.160
Fund positioning points
the other way, though.

69
00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.960
Kpler said in an earlier
note, dated the tenth,

70
00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.800
that trend-following funds cut their
Brent exposure from forty-five percent

71
00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:08.213
long to nine percent long in a single day.

72
00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:12.240
Their positions in gasoil and US
gasoline futures turned net short for

73
00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:15.040
the first time in more than four months.

74
00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.320
Refiners with diesel-heavy
output are the winners here.

75
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:22.080
If the Russian shortfall lasts, the
tight physical market and the short

76
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.960
funds could pull further apart.

77
00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.000
Over to gas. More US liquefied natural
gas cargoes have diverted toward

78
00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.880
Europe in recent days,
according to gCaptain.

79
00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.200
That adds supply to a tight market
and puts pressure on prices.

80
00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:40.347
Equinor, Europe's largest
pipeline gas supplier,

81
00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.720
is dealing with a cyberattack
on some of its IT systems.

82
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:47.400
The company says production is
unaffected and it has no sign that data

83
00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.120
was stolen.

84
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:51.680
British households face a harder winter.

85
00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.520
Cornwall Insight expects energy
bills to rise twenty-six percent from

86
00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:59.333
January. That would be the highest
level since twenty twenty-three.

87
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.840
In the US, the picture is easier.

88
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.440
Lower forty-eight gas storage ended
the injection season at about three

89
00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.040
point eight trillion cubic
feet, according to the EIA,

90
00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.000
almost two percent above
the five-year average.

91
00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.360
A few more things.

92
00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:17.840
EnQuest is selling its UK upstream
business to NEO NEXT Plus for up to

93
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.400
nine hundred and sixty million dollars.

94
00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:23.573
Eight hundred and forty million
of that is upfront cash.

95
00:05:23.627 --> 00:05:27.200
The sale includes Kraken, Magnus
and the Sullom Voe Terminal,

96
00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:30.720
and the business produced over thirty-one
thousand barrels of oil equivalent

97
00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.360
a day last year.

98
00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:36.400
Mozambique approved Exxon's
amended plan for Rovuma LNG,

99
00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:39.880
raising capacity to eighteen
point six million tonnes a year.

100
00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.040
That's up from fifteen point two.

101
00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.520
Exxon expects a final
investment decision by year-end.

102
00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.040
Woodside and Trafigura signed a deal
for one million tonnes a year of

103
00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:51.640
LNG, running for up to ten years.

104
00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.880
Supply starts in twenty thirty.

105
00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:57.600
Venture Global's twenty-year supply
deal with China Gas grows by five

106
00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:59.640
hundred thousand tonnes a year.

107
00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.600
And Hafnia has dropped
its pursuit of Torm.

108
00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.133
It plans to exit its nineteen
point nine percent stake.

109
00:06:06.187 --> 00:06:10.400
What to watch next. Daily EU gas
storage readings from Gas Infrastructure

110
00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.120
Europe run through the
twenty-fifth of November.

111
00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:16.880
And on the twenty-fifth, the EIA
weekly for the week to the twentieth

112
00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:20.040
shows whether distillate
stocks build for a third week.

113
00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:23.600
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
